{
  "caveats": [
    "Index values are neither rupee trade amounts nor physical tonnes. A value index combines price and volume effects; a volume index is a separate measure, and the two should not be added. Terms of trade below 100 refer to relative unit prices against the base and do not establish a trade deficit or declining trade volume. The excerpt does not give commodity weights, detailed coverage or seasonal adjustment. Published indices are rounded, so recomputing terms of trade from them can differ slightly from the reported figure. These national indices should not be joined to another base without a documented link.",
    "The source uses .. for unavailable figures and a dash for nil or negligible. Both retain their printed token and a distinct status; neither is converted to an exact zero."
  ],
